/-!
# Generation parameters: quotient transfer, rank reduction, and solvable groups

The extensions prove quotient-family and normalizer transport, lifting across
normal two-group kernels, reduction of any attained generation bound to m₂(G),
and rank-one generation for finite solvable groups (E.1.13). The local action
application uses the actual conjugation map on L/O₂(L). Actual cyclic
composition factors and their automorphism extensions are also certified.

General existence for even-order groups and the nonabelian composition-factor
reduction E.1.11 remain separate proof obligations. In particular the rank
bound retains its genuine existence hypothesis until final assembly.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, E.1.7 and E.1.11--13, pp.210--214.
-/
